@KOPRajs I found a subtle bug with the commit **[RetroPlayer: Do not rewrite manually created savestates with autosave](https://github.com/xbmc/xbmc/pull/22490/commits/42b7072a5531715bf1bffde2c0e89dade6d42ed0)**.

If an autosave is renamed, it still acts like an autosave, even though it looks like a manual save. So basically, the solution is to set the save type from auto to manual on rename. This is done with the following change:

```c++
--- a/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/savestates/SavestateDatabase.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/RetroPlayer/savestates/SavestateDatabase.cpp
@@ -175,7 +175,7 @@ bool CSavestateDatabase::RenameSavestate(const std::string& savestatePath, const

   newSavestate->SetLabel(label);
   newSavestate->SetCaption(savestate->Caption());
-  newSavestate->SetType(savestate->Type());
+  newSavestate->SetType(SAVE_TYPE::MANUAL); // Change autosave to manual save on rename
   newSavestate->SetCreated(savestate->Created());
   newSavestate->SetGameFileName(savestate->GameFileName());
   newSavestate->SetTimestampFrames(savestate->TimestampFrames());
```

I'm preparing a PR for in-game renaming/deleting. I'll include this change.
